{"name":"Harley Hair Purple","hex":"#8547b5","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"hair","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A pigmented filament of keratin which grows from a follicle on the skin of humans and other mammals.","The collection or mass of such growths growing from the skin of humans and animals, and forming a covering for any part or the whole body."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To remove the hair from.","To grow hair (where there was a bald spot)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hair"},{"term":"purple","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A colour between red and blue; violet, though often closer to magenta.","Any non-spectral colour on the line of purples on a colour chromaticity diagram or a colour wheel between violet and red."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a purple hue.","Not predominantly red or blue, but having a mixture of Democrat and Republican support."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/purple"}],"entries":[{"title":"Hair","blocks":[{"text":"Hair is a protein filament that grows from follicles found in the dermis. Hair is one of the distinguishing characteristics of mammals.\nThe human body, apart from areas of glabrous skin, is covered in follicles which produce thick terminal and fine vellus hair. Most common interest in hair is focused on hair growth, hair types, and hair care, but hair is also an important biomaterial primarily composed of protein, notably alpha-keratin."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/25/Gray945.png/330px-Gray945.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hair","wikidata":"Q28472"},{"title":"Purple","blocks":[{"text":"Purple is a color similar in appearance to violet light. In the RYB color model historically used in the arts, purple is a secondary color created by combining red and blue pigments. In the CMYK color model used in modern printing, purple is made by combining magenta pigment with cyan pigment, black pigment, or both. In the RGB color model used in computer and television screens, purple is created by mixing red and blue light in order to create colors that appear similar to violet light. According to color theory, purple is considered a cool color."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/Iris_sanguinea_cultivar%2C_Wakehurst_Place%2C_UK_-_Diliff.jpg/330px-Iris_sanguinea_cultivar%2C_Wakehurst_Place%2C_UK_-_Diliff.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Purple","wikidata":"Q3257809"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/CSIRO_ScienceImage_8115_Human_hair_and_Merino_wool_fibre.jpg/500px-CSIRO_ScienceImage_8115_Human_hair_and_Merino_wool_fibre.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/CSIRO_ScienceImage_8115_Human_hair_and_Merino_wool_fibre.jpg/1280px-CSIRO_ScienceImage_8115_Human_hair_and_Merino_wool_fibre.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/CSIRO_ScienceImage_8115_Human_hair_and_Merino_wool_fibre.jpg/500px-CSIRO_ScienceImage_8115_Human_hair_and_Merino_wool_fibre.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACSIRO_ScienceImage_8115_Human_hair_and_Merino_wool_fibre.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/68/506_Hair.jpg/500px-506_Hair.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/68/506_Hair.jpg/500px-506_Hair.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Anatomy of the hair shaft and bulb.","link":"https://en.wik